Scan TranslationInterface::translate() calls.

Potx does not look for translate(), so strings passed to an injected
TranslationInterface service - $this->translation->translate('...') - are never
extracted. We use that call form in enums and in services that inject the
translation service rather than using StringTranslationTrait.

This is deliberately not filed upstream. ContentEntityInterface::translate()
takes a langcode, and potx matches on a flat token stream, so a general version
of this would make potx extract langcodes such as 'da' as translatable strings
on any site that translates entities. It is only safe here because we do not
call translate() on entities. Grep before assuming that still holds.

--- a/potx.inc
+++ b/potx.inc
@@ -286,6 +286,9 @@
       // Drupal 8.
       _potx_find_t_calls_with_context($file_name, $save_callback, 'TranslatableMarkup');
       _potx_find_t_calls_with_context($file_name, $save_callback, 'TranslationWrapper');
+      // TranslationInterface::translate() on an injected translation service.
+      // Not covered upstream, see the header of this patch.
+      _potx_find_t_calls_with_context($file_name, $save_callback, 'translate');
     }
   }
   else {
